---
import CourseHome from '../../../../components/course/CourseHome.astro';
import '../../../../styles/lesson-kit.css';
import { ASTRONOMY } from '../../../../courses/astronomy/syllabus';
---
<CourseHome course={ASTRONOMY}>
  <p class="cs-meta"><strong>Quick reference:</strong> <a href="/learn/courses/astronomy/glossary/">glossary of terms</a> · <a href="/learn/courses/astronomy/cheat-sheet/">formula cheat sheet</a></p>
  <section class="cs-builds">
    <h2>What you will be able to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Read light like an astronomer</strong>: the spectrum, blackbodies, spectral lines, the Doppler shift and the inverse-square law.</li>
      <li><strong>Work out orbits</strong> with Kepler and Newton: periods, speeds, orbital elements, transfers and the planets.</li>
      <li><strong>Explain how stars work</strong>: distances by parallax, the HR diagram, fusion, binaries, Cepheids and how stars die.</li>
      <li><strong>Work like a researcher</strong>: photometry, periodograms, exoplanet fits, spectra, FITS files, open archives, error bars and how papers are written.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Every lesson starts with the big idea and what to read first, then gives you a step-by-step "watch it happen" player, a simulation to play with, a box on what each symbol means physically, a worked example, live problems with fresh numbers, hints and full solutions, a common mix-up, key points you can download as a summary sheet, a short quiz, and links to the free <a href="/science/astronomy/">astronomy tools</a> on fibub. To go out and look at the sky yourself, take <a href="/learn/courses/sky-watching/">Sky watching</a>. For the universe as a whole (its expansion, dark matter and the Big Bang), go on to <a href="/learn/courses/cosmology/">Cosmology</a>.</p>
  </section>
</CourseHome>
